      derive source code from the provided binaries.
    - Modify, bypass or forge licensing, trial, fingerprint or signature
      mechanisms.
    - Remove or alter the EULA, notices or integrity manifests.

Open-source components

The panel statically links and/or invokes third-party components that remain
under their own licenses. Notably:

  - ocserv            GPLv2 / LGPLv2+   shipped as source (ocserv-1.5.0.tar.xz)
                      and compiled on the target machine; sources are provided
                      in accordance with the GPL.
  - nginx, dnsmasq,   various FSF-approved / BSD licenses; installed from your
    iptables, ipset   distribution's packages, not from this repository.
  - Vue 3, Element Plus, ECharts, Pinia, vue-i18n  MIT License — distributed
    only in compiled/bundled form embedded within the panel binary.
  - gorilla/websocket, mattn/go-sqlite3, golang.org/x/crypto, golang.org/x/net
    MIT / BSD / Apache-2.0 — statically linked into the panel binary.

Source code for the GPL components is available in the release package. This
proprietary license does not restrict your rights under those GPL terms.

See EULA.txt for the full agreement. By installing or using this software you
accept it.
